cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EVALID: A Pre-Registered Identifiability Protocol"
message: "If you use this protocol or software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sosna
    given-names: Lukas A.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1266-9729"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
version: 0.3.7
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22545296"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LSosna/evalid"
abstract: >-
  EVALID is a pre-registered audit protocol for bounding how much of a reported
  empirical quantity can be produced without the capability it is claimed to
  evidence. Predictions, numeric thresholds and the resampling unit are fixed
  before data are loaded; passes and failures are both published; and every
  correction is logged rather than silently repaired. Version 0.3.2 adds a
  mandatory numerical uncertainty on every threshold comparison, an
  INDETERMINATE verdict state, a registered condition-number ceiling, and
  mandatory disclosure of self-audit.
keywords:
  - pre-registration
  - identifiability
  - degeneracy
  - benchmark evaluation
  - reproducibility
